  "sections": {
    "loc": {
      "type": "bella-location",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging for Texas home builders",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging for Home Builders in Texas",
        "lede": "Virtual staging for home builders is the digital furnishing of new construction photos: an interior designer places furniture and decor into photos of empty spec homes, quick move-ins and model plans, so prospective buyers can see how each room lives. Bella's designers stage Texas builder inventory in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo, and our 3D artists render the homes you haven't built yet from your plans.",
        "cta_label": "Stage a spec home — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "3D renderings from your plans",
        "alt_link": "/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization",
        "cred_text": "",
        "city": "Texas",
        "market_heading": "Virtual staging for home builders: Texas new construction, furnished online",
        "market_text": "<p>Texas builds more new homes than any other state. It led the country with 140,002 single-family permits in 2025, according to NAHB's analysis of Census Bureau data, and the Dallas and Houston metros issued more residential permits than any other US metro. That volume creates the builder's marketing problem: dozens of vacant spec homes and quick move-ins going live at once, several of them the same floor plan, all photographed empty.</p><p>Empty new construction photographs cold. White walls, bare floors and natural light bouncing off nothing make a four-bedroom plan look smaller than it is, and prospective buyers can't tell the flex room from the study. Virtually staged photos furnish each room to scale, so buyers understand the layout, how much furniture it really holds, and why this home beats the identical one two streets over.</p><p>A model home still earns its keep, but it shows one floor plan in one community. Traditional staging for every vacant spec home means a design fee and furniture rental per house, plus the logistics of moving furniture between new communities. Virtual staging services cost a fraction of that: {price:virtual-staging} a photo, paid once, with no rental clock running while a home waits for its buyer.</p><p>For homes that aren't built yet, the same team works from your plans. Our <a href=\"/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization\">3D rendering service</a> turns CAD or PDF drawings into photoreal exteriors, interiors and streetscapes from {price:3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization} a view, so sales can open before the slab is poured. The full builder playbook, from pre-sales to the last closing, is in our <a href=\"/pages/home-builder-marketing\">home builder marketing</a> guides.</p><p>Buyers decide online first: 83% of buyers' agents say staging makes it easier for a buyer to visualize the property as a future home (NAR, 2025 Profile of Home Staging). Staged photos are how Texas listings stand out when a buyer is scrolling a dozen new builds in the same ZIP code.</p>",
        "local_heading": "New construction in Houston, Austin, Dallas–Fort Worth and San Antonio",
        "local_text": "<p><strong>Houston.</strong> Master-planned communities in Katy, Cypress, The Woodlands and Sugar Land release single family homes in phases, and each phase needs listing photos the week it opens. Staged photos come back ready for the HAR.com MLS, with disclosure guidance.</p><p><strong>Dallas–Fort Worth.</strong> From Fort Worth to Frisco, Prosper, Celina and McKinney, DFW builders compete for relocation buyers who shortlist homes online before they fly in. Dallas listings upload to NTREIS; agents listing resale homes can see our <a href=\"/pages/virtual-staging-dallas\">virtual staging Dallas</a> page.</p><p><strong>Austin.</strong> Georgetown, Leander, Round Rock, Hutto and Kyle turn over spec inventory fast, and a clean modern style suits most of it. Files are ready for Unlock MLS.</p><p><strong>San Antonio.</strong> New Braunfels, Boerne, Schertz and the city's growth corridors are full of new builds that look alike online. Files are ready for LERA MLS, formerly the SABOR MLS.</p><p><strong>Luxury and custom builds.</strong> Custom builders in River Oaks, Highland Park and Westlake get the same designers at the same {price:virtual-staging} a photo. See <a href=\"/pages/luxury-virtual-staging\">luxury virtual staging</a> for how we stage high-end homes.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Texas markets we stage for builders",
        "hoods": "Houston, Katy, Cypress, The Woodlands, Frisco, Prosper, McKinney, Fort Worth, Austin, Georgetown, Leander, San Antonio, New Braunfels"
      }
    },
